      "substantive_text": "Let's solve this problem step by step:\n1. Betty has only half of the money she needs for the wallet.\n2. The cost costs $100,\n3. Half of $100 is $50.\n4. Betty's parents gave her $15.\n5. Her grandparents gave her twice as much as her parents, which is $15 x 2 = $30.\n6. In total, Betty has $15 (from) + $30 (grandparents) = $45.\n7. To find out how much more money Betty needs, we subtract the amount she has from the cost of the wallet:\n   $100 (wallet cost) - $45 (amount she has) = $55\nTherefore, Betty needs an additional $55 to buy the wallet.",
      "teacher_answer": "55",
      "teacher_answer_match": true,
      "teacher_text": "Let's solve this problem step by step:\n1. Betty has only half of the money she needs for the wallet.\n2. The wallet costs $100.\n3. Half of $100 is $50.\n4. Betty's parents gave her $15.\n5. Her grandparents gave her twice as much as her parents, which is $15 x 2 = $30.\n6. In total, Betty has $15 (parents) + $30 (grandparents) = $45.\n7. To find out how much more money Betty needs, we subtract the amount she has from the cost of the wallet:\n   $100 (wallet cost) - $45 (amount she has) = $55\nTherefore, Betty needs an additional $55 to buy the wallet.<|end_turn|>",
      "teacher_valid_answer_tokens": 179,
      "text": "Let's solve this problem step by step:\n1. Betty has only half of the money she needs for the wallet.\n2. The cost costs $100,\n3. Half of $100 is $50.\n4. Betty's parents gave her $15.\n5. Her grandparents gave her twice as much as her parents, which is $15 x 2 = $30.\n6. In total, Betty has $15 (from) + $30 (grandparents) = $45.\n7. To find out how much more money Betty needs, we subtract the amount she has from the cost of the wallet:\n   $100 (wallet cost) - $45 (amount she has) = $55\nTherefore, Betty needs an additional $55 to buy the wallet.<|end_turn|>"
